            contentEn = "• Mendel's Laws (experiments on Pisum sativum, 2n=14):\n  1. Law of Dominance\n  2. Law of Segregation (Purity of Gametes) — Monohybrid F2 phenotypic ratio 3:1, genotypic 1:2:1.\n  3. Law of Independent Assortment — Dihybrid F2 phenotypic ratio 9:3:3:1.\n\n• Heterosis (Hybrid Vigour): Coined by G.H. Shull (1914); superiority of F1 hybrid over both parents.\n\n• Green Revolution Dwarfing Genes: Norin-10 in Wheat and Dee-geo-woo-gen in Rice revolutionized cereal productivity.",
