            contentEn = "• Nutrient Content in Major Fertilizers:\n  1. Urea [CO(NH₂)₂]: 46% Nitrogen (Amide form). Hydrolyzed by urease enzyme in soil.\n  2. DAP (Diammonium Phosphate): 18% N and 46% P₂O₅.\n  3. SSP (Single Super Phosphate): 16% P₂O₅, 12% Sulphur, ~20% Calcium.\n  4. MOP (Muriate of Potash / KCl): 60% K₂O.\n\n• Cation Exchange Capacity (CEC): Capacity of soil colloids (clay & humus) to adsorb and exchange cations (Ca²⁺, Mg²⁺, K⁺, NH₄⁺). Humus has the highest CEC (150–300 cmol(p+)/kg).",
